  "configuration_id": "config_042",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_006 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is the best at 0.7250 acc / 0.6847 F1. scgpt is clearly inferior (0.52), resnet50 is inferior to imagenet_vit_l, and avgpool is inferior to transformer. The only major untested dimension in the top-performing regime is the RNA encoder: pca_n2000 (2000-dim linear) vs scvi_n200 (200-dim learned). config_042 pairs pca_n2000 with the proven-best image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), aggregation (transformer), and fusion (weighted), directly testing whether a higher-dimensional linear RNA representation can match or exceed the learned scvi embedding. This is the highest-value exploration remaining: it either finds a new best or confirms scvi_n200 is optimal, reducing uncertainty for the final 3 experiments. Expected cost is moderate (~3–4 GPU hours), similar to config_006's 3.60 hrs, since PCA encoding is cheap and the ViT-L + transformer pipeline dominates training time."
}

